cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the FinCrime Skills contracts, validator, or evaluation harness in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "FinCrime Skills: an evidence-contract capability layer for financial-crime AI agents"
abstract: >-
  FinCrime Skills is an open capability layer for AI agents operating in
  financial-crime environments. Its core artefact is the Evidence-Linked
  Finding: a structured contract in which every output claim is typed and
  bound to a specific, resolvable value in the supplied evidence. The project
  ships the normative contracts, a dependency-free deterministic validator, a
  native evaluation harness with no-skill baselines, and dated, cited,
  jurisdiction-scoped knowledge records. It provides risk reduction and
  evidence discipline; it does not provide regulatory assurance and makes no
  customer-facing decision.
type: software
